-> stack and heap memory
---------------------------
   Stack->stores method execution data->(local variables, method calls, references)
	->automatically allocated and deallocated as methods are called and return.
	->faster

   Heap ->stores objects and instance variables.
	->managed by java's Garbage Collector->which frees memory occupied by
	  unreachable objects.
	

public class Student {

    int age = 22;          // Instance variable -> Heap
    String name = "John";  // Instance variable -> Heap

    public void display() {
        int marks = 95;    // Local variable -> Stack

        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Marks: " + marks);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Student s1 = new Student(); // s1 -> Stack, Object -> Heap
        int id = 101;               // Local variable -> Stack

        s1.display();
    }
}

