Object/Class casting
-------------------------
Class casting is converting an object reference from one class type to another
   compatible class type.
 
 - upcasting   - Child object -> Parent reference
 - downcasting - Parent reference -> Child reference

note: to perform downcasting we have to do firstly upcasting

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Casting     | Syntax                 | Description                                   |
| ----------- | -----------------------| --------------------------------------------- |
| Upcasting   | Animal a = new Dog();  | Child object → Parent reference (implicit)    |
| Downcasting | Dog d = (Dog) a;`      | Parent reference → Child reference (explicit) |
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes a sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

public class CastingDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // -----------------------------
        // Upcasting: Child object -> Parent reference
        // -----------------------------
        Animal a = new Dog(); // Upcasting (implicit)
        a.sound();

        // a.bark(); // Compile-time Error
        // Parent reference cannot directly access child methods.

        // -----------------------------
        // Downcasting : Parent reference -> Child reference
        // -----------------------------
        Dog d = (Dog) a; // Downcasting (explicit)
        d.sound();
        d.bark();
    }
}

Output
------
Animal makes a sound
Animal makes a sound
Dog barks


