# Autoboxing & Unboxing
-----------------------
Java is an object-oriented language, but it also supports primitive data types.
Autoboxing and Unboxing bridge the gap between primitives and objects.

-> Autoboxing - converting a primitive value into its corresponding wrapper object automatically
   int num = 100; 	             // Primitive
   Integer i = num; 		     // Autoboxing
   Integer j = Integer.valueOf(num); // Explicit conversion

-> Unboxing - converting a wrapper object into its corresponding primitive value automatically.
   Integer i = 100;		// Wrapper Object
   int num = i;			// Unboxing
   int num = i.intValue();	// Explicit unboxing

	Primitive---Autoboxing--->Wrapper class----Unboxing--->Unboxing

Example:
	int a = 50 	 // primitive
	Integer b = a 	 // autoboxing (valueOf())
	Integer c = 200  // wrapper object
	int d = c	 // unboxing (intValue())


