HashMap is a class that implements the Map interface.
It stores data as key:value pairs and uses hashing for
   fast insertion, deletion, and lookup.
it uses a hash function to determine the index(bucket) to store the key
if multiple keys map to the same index (collision),
collision handle-
Linked List	-> before java 8
Red-Black Tree	-> java 8+  -> to improve performace
        (Black)
          10
        /    \
     (R)5    (R)20
      / \       \
   (B)2 (B)7   (B)30


" A HashMap converts a bucket's linked list into a Red-Black Tree only
when more than 8 entries are present in the same bucket and the HashMap's
capacity is at least 64."

Threshold Value in HashMap
--------------------------
The threshold is the maximum number of entries a HashMap can
hold before it resizes (rehashes).
	Formula: Threshold = Capacity × Load Factor

Default Values:
    Initial Capacity: 16
    Load Factor: 0.75

	Threshold = 16 × 0.75 = 12

"This means when the 13th element is inserted, the HashMap resizes."



-> How does HashMap work internally?
------------------------------------
Uses hashCode() to find bucket
Uses equals() to check key inside bucket
Stores data in array of buckets


-> HashMap key-features
-----------------------
stores data -> key-value pair
keys -> unique,	null key  -> one
values -> duplicate,	null values-> multiple
order -> not guarantee any order


