-> TreeMap implements both SortedMap and SequencedMap because they represent
different concepts.
-----------------------------------------------
SortedMap answers: How are the keys ordered?
Keys are sorted according to their natural ordering or a Comparator.
It provides sorting-specific methods like subMap(), headMap(), tailMap(),
firstKey(), and lastKey().

SequencedMap answers: Can I traverse the map from first to last (and in reverse)?
It provides a common API for ordered maps, such as firstEntry(), lastEntry(),
reversed(), and sequencedKeySet().



-> To reverse a TreeMap in Java
