Stream API
###########
----------------
What is Stream?
----------------
A stream  is a sequence of elements that supports functional-style operations.
not a data structure
does not store data
operations are pipelined
lazy evaluation
can be processed in parallel

--------------------
Types Of Operations
--------------------
INTERMEDIATE: Return a stream(can be chained)
	filter(),map(),sorted(),distinct(),limit(),skip(),peek(),flatMap(), etc.

TERMINAL: Return a result or side-effect
	forEach(),collect(),reduce(),count(),anyMatch(),allMatch(),findFirst(),ect.

SHORT-CIRCUIT: May not process all elements
	anyMatch(),allMatch(),findFirst(),findAny(),limit(), etc


3. CREATE STREAM
--------------------
list.stream();		// from collection
Arrays.stream(arr); 	// from array
Stream.of(1,2,3,4); 	// from values
list.parallelStream();  // from parallel stream ->note: use only when working with large data & idependent operations


4. INTERMEDIATE OPERATIONS (Return Stream)
------------------------------------------------
filter(): selects elements that match the condition
	List<Integer> even=nums.stream().filter(n->n%2==0).toList(); //[2,4,6]
map(): transforms each element
	List<Integer> squares=nums.stream().map(n->n*n).toList(); //[1,4,9,16,25,36]
flatMap(): Flattens nested structures
	List<List<Integer>> list=List.of(list.of(1,2),List.of(3,4);
	List<Integer> flat=list.stream().flatMap(List::stream).toList(); //[1,2,3,4]
